WEBVTT

00:02.650 --> 00:05.150
A date with me?

00:06.710 --> 00:08.200
I'm surprised.

00:08.200 --> 00:10.360
Where did that come from, Shin?

00:10.730 --> 00:11.980
Is that a no?

00:11.980 --> 00:15.750
We should still have a whole day 
before DEM's assault.

00:15.750 --> 00:20.360
That's true, but there's 
no need to train for that, right?

00:20.360 --> 00:21.980
This isn't for training!

00:23.050 --> 00:27.060
With the final battle drawing near,

00:27.060 --> 00:29.330
that's all the more reason 
I want to invite you on a date.

00:30.890 --> 00:33.510
Do the others know?

00:33.970 --> 00:35.030
I haven't told them.

00:35.740 --> 00:38.010
Why me?

00:38.410 --> 00:39.760
You don't want to?

00:40.050 --> 00:41.970
I haven't said that,

00:41.970 --> 00:45.600
but if you wanted to go on a date with someone,

00:45.600 --> 00:47.400
then you should have other options.

00:47.400 --> 00:49.300
That won't do.

00:49.300 --> 00:51.950
I want to go on a date with you, Reine.

00:55.650 --> 00:57.340
I'll make some time.

00:57.810 --> 00:59.670
Where should we go?

02:33.710 --> 02:34.780
I see.

02:35.630 --> 02:38.510
Reine is your best friend.

02:39.050 --> 02:43.690
I'm sure you're shocked to hear 
all of this so suddenly, but...

02:45.930 --> 02:47.210
Thank you.

02:47.210 --> 02:49.240
I'm sure it was hard for you, too.

02:49.240 --> 02:51.210
Thank you for telling me.

02:51.210 --> 02:52.250
Kotori...

02:52.690 --> 02:57.150
<i>Well then, let's come up with 
a strategy without Reine noticing.</i>

02:58.170 --> 03:00.220
Yeah, let's do that.

03:00.980 --> 03:05.910
To start, we'll have to think of 
what to do for Reine's date by morning,

03:06.220 --> 03:10.670
all while simultaneously 
preparing our strategies against DEM.

03:11.300 --> 03:13.500
That's true, also...

03:14.500 --> 03:16.210
Deal with the other Spirits?

03:16.210 --> 03:17.180
Yeah.

03:17.830 --> 03:22.390
Reine was a reliable older sister 
they all could trust.

03:22.790 --> 03:25.900
When they learn that she betrayed them...

03:27.260 --> 03:28.650
True.

03:28.650 --> 03:30.770
Though we'll need them to get over that.

03:33.060 --> 03:35.310
Origami Tobiichi
 Cell Phone
 Calling
 Answer Cancel

03:33.370 --> 03:34.420
Origami?

03:37.310 --> 03:39.200
I heard what's going on.

03:39.200 --> 03:39.770
Huh?

03:40.220 --> 03:42.740
<i>I've informed all the Spirits, too.</i>

03:42.740 --> 03:45.960
<i>We'll help you compose your date plan.</i>

03:45.960 --> 03:47.580
H-Hold on a moment.

03:47.580 --> 03:49.180
You heard?

03:49.180 --> 03:50.590
How did you...?

03:52.180 --> 03:54.700
Shido, your second button.

03:54.700 --> 03:55.460
Huh?

03:55.820 --> 03:56.960
Ah!

03:58.460 --> 04:00.460
I understand what's going on!

04:00.930 --> 04:03.220
I heard the details from Origami.

04:03.610 --> 04:06.850
That was a surprise, 
but there's no time to be depressed.

04:07.140 --> 04:11.260
Now these are some hot developments 
happening without my knowledge!

04:11.260 --> 04:13.600
I kind of like this stuff!

04:14.700 --> 04:16.740
Impressive, Reine Murasame!

04:16.740 --> 04:19.440
You managed to deceive Kaguya Yamai!

04:19.440 --> 04:23.240
Petition. Please let us help you, too.

04:23.630 --> 04:25.010
All right.

04:25.010 --> 04:27.290
Then assemble in the briefing room.

04:27.700 --> 04:31.970
Go one at a time so Reine 
doesn't catch on if you run into her.

04:32.940 --> 04:35.540
Kotori, could you give me a bit of time?

04:35.540 --> 04:36.380
Huh?

04:36.820 --> 04:39.140
There's something I have to do.

04:43.740 --> 04:44.870
I want to talk.

04:45.670 --> 04:47.410
You're there, right, Kurumi?

04:54.210 --> 04:55.690
You, huh?

04:56.000 --> 04:59.530
My, my, this is unusual.

04:59.530 --> 05:02.940
You're actually summoning me for once.

05:03.460 --> 05:05.590
Are you the only one here right now?

05:06.010 --> 05:08.740
Is the real Kurumi listening 
into this conversation?

05:09.100 --> 05:11.700
You ask quite the odd question.

05:11.700 --> 05:17.540
None of the other clones 
or the real me are here.

05:17.540 --> 05:21.930
If you want to discuss something 
you don't want the real me to hear,

05:21.930 --> 05:24.420
then you're safe on that front.

05:25.170 --> 05:26.330
I see.

05:27.170 --> 05:33.530
I don't know if what I'm about to tell you 
is safe to pass on to the real Kurumi.

05:34.140 --> 05:37.630
So could you listen 
and make that decision for me?

05:39.820 --> 05:42.860
On February 20th, the real Kurumi

05:43.380 --> 05:44.500
will die.

05:46.580 --> 05:49.900
You speak like you've actually seen it happen.

05:49.900 --> 05:52.370
Yeah, your guess is correct.

05:52.780 --> 05:56.340
Who are you suggesting 
managed to take me down?

05:56.340 --> 05:59.940
Even if I'm about to face Ellen Mathers,

05:59.940 --> 06:04.380
I won't go down that easily, you know.

06:04.950 --> 06:07.010
It was Mio Takamiya.

06:08.380 --> 06:11.130
The Spirit of Origin will kill Kurumi.

06:11.530 --> 06:15.570
Mio suddenly appeared from within 
Kurumi on the future battlefield.

06:16.370 --> 06:19.980
I believe Mio is already inside of Kurumi.

06:21.180 --> 06:23.280
So that's what happens.

06:24.100 --> 06:25.970
I'm grateful.

06:26.460 --> 06:31.410
You're right, this isn't information 
to be handled carelessly.

06:31.810 --> 06:32.960
So?

06:32.960 --> 06:36.790
Do you think you can convey this 
to Kurumi without Mio catching wind of it?

06:37.170 --> 06:38.860
Most likely, yes.

06:38.860 --> 06:43.790
Though, the real problem is 
what to do about it afterwards.

06:44.090 --> 06:45.540
Right.

06:45.540 --> 06:47.940
I hope there's something 
I can do to help, but...

06:49.940 --> 06:53.190
Please don't make such a sad face.

06:53.690 --> 06:57.890
I know this is a desperate situation,

06:57.890 --> 07:01.870
but thanks to you I now have options.

07:04.650 --> 07:10.070
Shido, was I able to fulfill 
my duty in the future?

07:11.830 --> 07:14.730
Yeah, in the coolest way possible.

07:16.510 --> 07:17.980
Is that so?

07:33.260 --> 07:36.180
R-Reine?! What are you doing?!

07:36.710 --> 07:38.290
Working.

07:38.290 --> 07:41.570
I figured I would take care of 
tomorrow's work, too.

07:42.060 --> 07:43.810
I finally finished up.

07:43.810 --> 07:45.210
I see!

07:45.210 --> 07:46.480
Good work, then!

07:46.480 --> 07:49.280
And what are you up to at this hour, Tohka?

07:49.280 --> 07:51.950
W-Well, um, uh...

07:52.780 --> 07:54.100
If you want a late-night snack,

07:54.100 --> 07:56.740
you should go to the cafeteria 
or the break area.

07:57.290 --> 08:01.210
Though go easy on the snacks, 
given how late it is.

08:01.740 --> 08:04.480
And don't forget to 
brush your teeth before bed.

08:04.480 --> 08:06.960
Y-Yes, I'll be careful.

08:07.490 --> 08:09.420
I understand why you can't sleep,

08:09.420 --> 08:11.410
but make sure to get rest.

08:12.030 --> 08:17.330
We have to do everything we can 
to protect Shin from DEM, after all.

08:18.820 --> 08:19.830
Reine.

08:20.150 --> 08:20.970
Hmm?

08:21.340 --> 08:24.480
Reine... do you like Shido?

08:24.480 --> 08:25.350
Huh?

08:26.270 --> 08:27.890
What do you mean?

08:27.890 --> 08:30.380
Just answer the question. Please.

08:31.260 --> 08:33.310
Yeah, I like him.

08:35.140 --> 08:38.330
I see. Yeah. Me, too!

08:47.180 --> 08:50.170
No, I'm overthinking it.

08:52.510 --> 09:01.140
Amamiya Station

08:53.100 --> 08:54.460
<i>Hello, Shido.</i>

08:54.460 --> 08:57.170
<i>How's the bone conduction receiver working?</i>

08:57.170 --> 08:58.540
I can hear you clearly.

08:58.540 --> 09:01.140
Though it is slightly different than usual.

09:01.480 --> 09:04.380
<i>Reine would catch on 
if we used the usual transceiver.</i>

09:04.810 --> 09:07.530
<i>We won't have to worry about 
her noticing with this.</i>

09:07.530 --> 09:10.240
<i>She should be arriving soon, so get ready.</i>

09:10.240 --> 09:11.150
All right.

09:11.620 --> 09:13.890
Hey, did I keep you waiting?

09:16.410 --> 09:18.980
R-Reine?!

09:33.060 --> 09:35.050
It's finally starting.

09:36.410 --> 09:40.710
Now, let our date begin.

09:49.120 --> 09:51.900
Honestly, I still can't believe it.

09:52.350 --> 09:54.940
Our Reine is Phantom?

09:55.320 --> 09:57.280
I feel the same way.

09:57.280 --> 09:59.820
But we have to accept the facts.

10:01.490 --> 10:03.900
Still, it's not something 
to be pessimistic about.

10:03.900 --> 10:09.580
According to the boy, the friendship 
she feels toward us is the real deal, too.

10:09.580 --> 10:11.340
Exactly.

10:11.810 --> 10:15.140
So in short, as long as Shido can make 
Reine fall for him and seal her power,

10:15.140 --> 10:17.220
then all of this will be resolved peacefully.

10:17.790 --> 10:20.020
What's the matter, Shin?

10:20.020 --> 10:22.020
Did I shock you that much?

10:22.020 --> 10:24.100
Oh, no, um...

10:24.140 --> 10:26.640
<b>1) I'm sorry, I was captivated by you.</b>

10:24.720 --> 10:26.640
<b>2) That's not your usual hairstyle, is it? It's lovely.</b>

10:25.350 --> 10:26.640
<b>3) What'll it take to let me strip that outfit off of you?</b>

10:26.640 --> 10:28.310
Everyone, choices!

10:28.310 --> 10:29.690
Yeah!

10:31.940 --> 10:33.240
1, huh?

10:33.240 --> 10:34.690
That's most reasonable.

10:35.040 --> 10:36.000
Yes.

10:36.000 --> 10:39.820
I think going silent 
would only make her anxious.

10:39.820 --> 10:42.950
But if he says that, she'll be happy.

10:42.950 --> 10:46.530
Huh? Such consideration! Are you a goddess?

10:46.530 --> 10:49.420
What does it say about me 
that I chose the other

10:49.420 --> 10:51.830
because I think we should wait and see for now.

10:51.830 --> 10:55.460
Yes, I think Reine 
will approve of this one, too!

10:55.910 --> 11:00.380
Hmm. I don't think 2 is a bad choice either.

11:00.380 --> 11:01.970
Well, whatever.

11:01.970 --> 11:03.320
Indeed!

11:03.320 --> 11:05.100
God dwells in the details.

11:05.100 --> 11:08.920
It's important to notice 
the minor changes, but...

11:08.920 --> 11:11.300
Addendum. Depending on the person,

11:11.300 --> 11:15.370
some might take it as suggesting 
their usual hairstyle isn't that great.

11:15.370 --> 11:18.490
I think we should play it safe 
and wait and see.

11:19.580 --> 11:21.990
So, what do you three think?

11:22.290 --> 11:25.450
No, it's clearly 3 here!

11:25.450 --> 11:28.500
Hearing such a surprising comeback 
from such an innocent young boy

11:28.500 --> 11:30.370
would really turn a lady on!

11:30.810 --> 11:32.400
Right!

11:32.400 --> 11:34.860
Reine is a mature woman, too,

11:34.860 --> 11:38.130
so she'll appreciate wit like that.

11:38.520 --> 11:40.020
Listen...

11:40.020 --> 11:44.260
our future is riding on this, 
so could you please take this seriously?

11:44.900 --> 11:46.230
We know.

11:46.230 --> 11:50.770
That's why we chose the line that 
would make us the happiest to hear.

11:52.660 --> 11:54.770
Shido, go with 1.

11:55.270 --> 11:57.730
Oh, I'm sorry.

11:57.730 --> 12:02.050
I've never seen you dressed 
like this before, so well...

12:02.550 --> 12:04.280
I was captivated.

12:04.780 --> 12:05.540
Hmm?

12:06.610 --> 12:08.130
I see.

12:08.130 --> 12:10.460
Hmm, is that so?

12:11.290 --> 12:12.500
Thank you.

12:12.500 --> 12:14.420
Your outfit is wonderful, too.

12:14.420 --> 12:16.920
Th-Thank you.

12:17.300 --> 12:20.180
Now, where are we going today?

12:20.180 --> 12:22.500
It looks like you brought a lot of luggage?

12:22.500 --> 12:24.170
That's still a secret for now.

12:24.170 --> 12:25.980
I want to surprise you.

12:26.510 --> 12:29.220
Will you trust me and follow along?

12:29.220 --> 12:30.910
Yes, of course.

12:31.740 --> 12:33.180
Shall we go, then?

12:33.900 --> 12:35.190
What's the matter?

12:35.870 --> 12:38.660
This is technically a date, right?

12:38.660 --> 12:41.940
Yes, it is. No technically about it.

12:42.340 --> 12:44.450
Hmm, in that case...

12:55.510 --> 12:56.710
Shall we go?

12:57.380 --> 12:58.110
Yes.

13:00.930 --> 13:04.700
Her affection rating... 
is a strange wave pattern.

13:04.700 --> 13:08.800
It looks like she holds enough affection 
for us to be able to seal her at any moment,

13:08.800 --> 13:11.600
but it's not triggering 
the possibility to seal her.

13:11.880 --> 13:14.250
It's like she holds deep affection for him,

13:14.250 --> 13:16.780
but she's keeping herself at a distance.

13:16.780 --> 13:18.700
Almost like she's affectionately 
watching over him from the sidelines

13:18.700 --> 13:21.360
while everyone else 
gets to be on stage with him.

13:21.680 --> 13:24.360
One could also say it's like a mother?

13:24.810 --> 13:27.690
I see, that's oddly well put.

13:27.690 --> 13:31.970
Either way, it doesn't change the fact 
she'll be a difficult target.

13:35.330 --> 13:36.370
This is...

13:36.370 --> 13:39.000
Reine's affection is climbing!

13:39.280 --> 13:41.630
Looks like your strategy 
is working, Commander!

13:42.010 --> 13:44.260
It wasn't solely my idea.

13:44.700 --> 13:49.010
It's the result of all of us spirits 
ironing out a plan until late last night.

13:49.410 --> 13:52.060
A day trip to a hot springs inn on the weekend?

13:52.060 --> 13:55.020
This really is an attractive choice.

13:55.020 --> 14:00.480
Analyst Murasame is the one 
who works the most in Fraxinus, too.

14:00.480 --> 14:04.650
She also works as a teacher 
at Raizen High on top of that.

14:04.650 --> 14:11.410
She's also been working to revive 
Shinji Takamiya for decades as well.

14:11.410 --> 14:14.910
Even if she is a Spirit, it's only 
natural that's she built up fatigue.

14:15.180 --> 14:19.540
Reine always does have bags under her eyes.

14:19.540 --> 14:22.790
I thought she must be struggling with her work.

14:22.790 --> 14:26.800
I'm sure she doesn't get 
much sleep every night.

14:26.800 --> 14:30.430
Her mind and body should both 
be completely exhausted.

14:30.430 --> 14:33.930
So what Reine needs is relaxation!

14:34.340 --> 14:36.880
She can use the various relaxation services

14:36.880 --> 14:40.190
to relieve her pent up weariness and fatigue!

14:42.410 --> 14:43.390
Oh!

14:44.320 --> 14:46.440
<b>1) Take it easy and stretch out in the large bath</b>

14:44.900 --> 14:46.440
<b>2) Relax in the private outdoor bath</b>

14:45.530 --> 14:46.440
<b>3) Get a refreshing massage</b>

14:46.770 --> 14:48.190
Everyone, choices!

14:48.530 --> 14:49.570
Yeah!

14:52.170 --> 14:54.080
Hmm, yeah, 2.

14:54.440 --> 15:01.830
Yes, though I don't feel good about Reine 
and Shido taking a bath alone together.

15:02.180 --> 15:03.000
Yes.

15:03.000 --> 15:07.460
I think they both need to 
be able to talk a lot.

15:07.850 --> 15:12.740
It's okay. I'm calm. I'm calm. I'm calm.

15:12.740 --> 15:15.450
Huh? Why did you need to say that thrice?

15:15.450 --> 15:20.490
Besides, I've been alone 
in the bath with Shido, too.

15:20.490 --> 15:24.150
I shouldn't be losing my calm 
over something like this.

15:24.150 --> 15:25.190
Hold on!

15:25.190 --> 15:28.650
That was when you were lying in wait 
to ambush him, wasn't it?!

15:29.830 --> 15:32.940
You can't leave us Yamai sisters out 
when it comes to bathing.

15:32.940 --> 15:34.100
Affirmative.

15:34.100 --> 15:39.040
Sandwiching Shido between me 
and Kaguya was a nice memory.

15:39.040 --> 15:42.040
They should be spending 
some time naked together

15:42.040 --> 15:44.420
since they're at a hot springs inn!

15:44.420 --> 15:47.420
Right in a bath tub about this big!

15:47.420 --> 15:50.300
Both Darling and Reine packed in tight!

15:50.300 --> 15:56.050
It's the world's greatest packed lunch!

15:56.370 --> 15:58.180
Shido, go with 2.

15:58.470 --> 15:59.680
Roger.

16:08.890 --> 16:11.560
Shin, can I come in?

16:11.560 --> 16:13.790
Oh, yes, go ahead.

16:15.420 --> 16:16.030
Wha?!

16:16.450 --> 16:17.530
Wha?!

16:18.640 --> 16:19.830
Whoa!

16:19.830 --> 16:22.080
What is the meaning of this?!

16:22.080 --> 16:23.730
I can't see Analyst Murasame's na—

16:23.730 --> 16:26.580
No, I can't see our important conquest screen!

16:26.580 --> 16:30.460
Dear god! Bring it back at once!

16:31.060 --> 16:34.820
<i>Our objective is to make 
the Spirit fall for him.</i>

16:34.820 --> 16:36.820
<i>I believe it best to avoid doing things</i>

16:36.820 --> 16:40.350
<i>Reine would find unpleasant 
after we've sealed her spirit power.</i>

16:40.350 --> 16:42.680
No!

16:45.010 --> 16:47.630
Kannazuki, you're still calm.

16:48.900 --> 16:49.850
Yes.

16:49.850 --> 16:53.740
Because I don't have 
much interest in big breasts.

16:54.300 --> 16:55.410
That so?

16:59.460 --> 17:02.250
We're all alone, so you don't mind, right?

17:02.620 --> 17:04.750
N-No...

17:05.470 --> 17:07.330
<i>Those are quite something...</i>

17:11.110 --> 17:13.630
Um, Reine,

17:14.070 --> 17:16.380
how long have you been with Ratatoskr?

17:16.780 --> 17:19.070
It was around five or six years ago?

17:19.070 --> 17:23.260
It was around the same time 
Kotori became the commander.

17:23.260 --> 17:24.530
I see.

17:25.330 --> 17:28.020
You know, thank you.

17:28.450 --> 17:29.570
For what?

17:29.570 --> 17:33.540
Well, that means you've been 
supporting Kotori all this time.

17:35.820 --> 17:37.820
I haven't done anything that important.

17:38.310 --> 17:42.910
I'm sure she would be a great 
commander even without me.

17:43.210 --> 17:50.040
Well, I won't deny that Kotori is talented, 
but what did you do before then?

17:50.360 --> 17:52.430
I was your typical student.

17:52.430 --> 17:57.050
My thesis got recognition, 
so I was scouted for Ratatoskr.

18:00.300 --> 18:03.010
Was there anyone you fell in love with?

18:06.590 --> 18:08.810
There was one person.

18:13.340 --> 18:14.550
Was that...?

18:15.700 --> 18:19.050
It's not fair to talk about just me.

18:19.540 --> 18:22.090
Would you tell me more about yourself, too?

18:22.090 --> 18:22.770
Huh?

18:23.490 --> 18:25.260
S-Sure.

18:25.690 --> 18:29.660
I've been wanting to hear more 
about you for a long time, too.

18:30.220 --> 18:34.850
Do you remember anything that happened 
before you were taken in by the Itsuka family?

18:38.890 --> 18:42.780
Honestly, I don't really have 
any clear memories.

18:43.290 --> 18:44.600
What I do remember...

18:45.030 --> 18:47.610
is the sensation of being held by warm hands,

18:47.610 --> 18:51.010
and a sense of loss like those hands 
were leaving me behind.

18:51.660 --> 18:52.610
I'm sure...

18:53.000 --> 18:55.210
that must have been my mother.

18:57.130 --> 19:00.610
Do you resent your mother for abandoning you?

19:00.930 --> 19:01.540
Huh?

19:02.780 --> 19:05.870
I don't resent her or anything.

19:06.490 --> 19:09.870
I'm sure she had her reasons for it.

19:10.310 --> 19:13.060
I doubt she abandoned me because she wanted to.

19:14.030 --> 19:16.340
Besides, I remember.

19:16.890 --> 19:20.230
I remember how kind 
the hands that held me were.

19:21.570 --> 19:22.570
I see...

19:32.850 --> 19:33.570
Huh?

19:34.850 --> 19:36.330
There, there.

19:37.000 --> 19:39.650
Hey, Reine?!

19:40.180 --> 19:42.220
A little of this won't hurt, will it?

19:42.770 --> 19:45.940
Though I may not be able to replace her.

19:50.530 --> 19:53.520
<i>Ellen, sorry for the suddenness,</i>

19:53.520 --> 19:55.650
<i>but I've decided to speed up our plans.</i>

19:56.220 --> 19:58.020
<i>The situation has changed.</i>

19:58.020 --> 20:01.560
<i>Rather, it seems it's about to change.</i>

20:01.560 --> 20:03.680
What do you mean, Ike?

20:04.050 --> 20:08.220
<i>Honestly, I really am fortunate.</i>

20:08.220 --> 20:10.500
<i>Never before have I felt like it was destiny</i>

20:10.500 --> 20:16.060
<i>that the omniscient Beelzebub 
was the first Demon King I obtained.</i>

20:16.400 --> 20:20.330
Meaning you've learned 
some new fact through Beelzebub?

20:20.770 --> 20:22.690
<i>Precisely.</i>

20:22.690 --> 20:27.380
<i>Apparently we've already suffered 
painful defeat once before.</i>

20:27.380 --> 20:29.930
<i>In a future unknown to us.</i>

20:31.060 --> 20:34.850
However, this time we can strike first.

20:35.250 --> 20:37.960
Start preparing the magic reactor.

20:38.610 --> 20:41.370
<i>We'll want absorption charms as well.</i>

20:42.660 --> 20:44.720
Then the Spirit of Origin...?

20:45.310 --> 20:47.460
Come on, Ellen.

20:47.460 --> 20:51.690
Let's change the future as well.

21:11.650 --> 21:14.390
What is it you wanted to show me, Shin?

21:15.010 --> 21:16.210
We're almost there.

21:16.750 --> 21:18.500
I'm sure you'll like it.

21:21.340 --> 21:22.380
We're here.

21:22.790 --> 21:24.470
You can open your eyes now.

21:35.340 --> 21:36.270
This is!

21:36.820 --> 21:39.070
This is the place I wanted to show you, Reine.

21:39.470 --> 21:40.590
It's pretty, right?

21:46.820 --> 21:49.530
Yes, it is pretty.

21:50.110 --> 21:51.130
Very much so.

21:52.740 --> 21:55.000
<b>Episode 9</b>

21:52.740 --> 21:55.000
<b>A "Second" Date</b>

23:25.000 --> 23:40.020
Episode 10: "A Battlefield That Shouldn't Be Possible"

23:26.260 --> 23:28.690
The final battle with Westcott is here.

23:28.690 --> 23:32.390
Who will seize the future? DEM? Or Ratatoskr?

23:32.800 --> 23:34.380
Next time is Episode 10:

23:34.380 --> 23:36.300
"A Battlefield That Shouldn't Be Possible."

23:36.890 --> 23:39.210
All three siblings have gathered.
